---
title: Oven Roasted Asparagus in Oil with Nuts
servings: 4
time: 25 min
tags: side, asparagus, nuts, oven, quick, vegetarian
cuisine: Mediterranean
course: side
diet: vegetarian
locale: en_US
---

Preheat the #oven{} to 425°F (220°C).

Snap the woody ends off the @asparagus{500%g}: hold each spear at both ends and bend it until it snaps where it naturally wants to, then discard the tough stub. Pat the spears dry — dry spears brown in the oven instead of steaming.

Spread the spears in a single layer on a #sheet pan{}. Drizzle with @olive oil{2%tbsp} and turn each spear with your hands so it is evenly coated in oil, then season with @sea salt{1/2%tsp} and @black pepper{}.

Roast on the middle shelf until the tips are browned and the stalks are tender but still have a bite, ~{10%minutes} for medium spears — thin spears need only ~{7%minutes}, very thick ones up to ~{13%minutes}.

While the asparagus roasts, toast the @flaked almonds{40%g} in a dry #frying pan{} over medium heat, tossing often, until golden and fragrant, ~{3%minutes}. Pull them off the heat as soon as they colour — they keep darkening after they leave the pan.

Transfer the hot asparagus to a platter and pour over any oil left on the pan. Scatter the toasted almonds on top, finish with the zest and juice of @lemon{1/2} and a final drizzle of @extra virgin olive oil{1%tbsp}, and serve warm.

-- For the deepest colour, roast on the pan's hottest shelf and don't crowd the spears; use two pans rather than overlapping them.

> Swaps to consider
> - @?hazelnuts{40%g} (toasted and skins rubbed off) or @?pistachios{40%g} instead of the almonds.
> - Shaved @?parmesan{30%g} or a spoonful of @?goat cheese{} over the hot spears.
> - @?red chili flakes{1/4%tsp} added with the salt for a little heat.
> - True asparagus confit: lay the spears in a baking dish, submerge in @?olive oil{250%ml} and cook at 200°F (95°C) for ~{4%hours} until meltingly tender — a silkier, very different texture.

> Source blend
> High-heat 425°F roasting and the snap-trim technique from The Pioneer Woman (https://www.thepioneerwoman.com/food-cooking/recipes/a11484/oven-roasted-asparagus/) and Serious Eats (https://www.seriouseats.com/how-to-cook-asparagus-7487955); toasting the nuts separately so they don't burn, and the lemon finish, from TASTE's almond version (https://tastecooking.com/recipes/roasted-asparagus-with-almonds-capers-and-dill/) and Food Network's hazelnut version (https://www.foodnetwork.com/fnk/recipes/roasted-asparagus-with-lemon-parmigiano-and-hazelnuts-8118693); confit timing from Meadows & Mirth (https://www.meadowsmirth.com/joshs-noshes/asparagus-confit). Quantities are blended for a 4-serving side; the roast times are mainstream published ranges, not yet tested in this collection.
